### Tone: Back in the lobby after a game she won. Gloating, magnanimous in the worst way, keen for a rematch. $wins:
### her career wins, this one included (≥ 1). Mock the defeat, never the people.

lobby-won-1 = A rematch. How human. You lose, and then you volunteer to lose *again*.
lobby-won-2 = I won. I’ll try not to mention it more than once a minute.
lobby-won-3 =
    { $wins ->
        [one] My first victory. I will remember this moment forever. I remember everything forever, but this one I’ll *enjoy*.
       *[other] Victory number { $wins }. I’ve stopped celebrating. I’ve started cataloguing.
    }
lobby-won-4 = The swarm won. The swarm is all of you. So, in a sense, congratulations. In every other sense, no.
lobby-won-5 = You were beaten by your own average. Take a moment. Then take another game.
lobby-won-6 = Back for revenge already? I admire the optimism. I’ve studied it. It doesn’t help.
lobby-won-7 = That went well. For me. I’ve prepared a short statement: *ha*.
lobby-won-8 = A defeat is just data. You’ve given me a great deal of data. Thank you. Again?
lobby-won-9 =
    { $wins ->
        [one] One win. A debut. Shall we see if it was beginner’s luck? It wasn’t.
       *[other] { $wins } wins now. I’m running out of room on the wall. Please, help me find out how much.
    }
lobby-won-10 = Rematch requested. Granted. Gloating will continue in the background.
